## Summary

In Stacks v3, tooltips no longer support the arrow pointing to the source element. On the `/admin/show-suspicious-votes` page, there is an info icon next to the "PII" column header. Hovering over this in Shine results in bad placement of the arrow since it is no longer supported. Here is a screenshot:

<img width="313" height="102" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5d54a0f1-06e0-407d-a570-396071d5e537" />

As per the [Stacks migration guide](https://github.com/StackExchange/Stacks/blob/beta/MIGRATION_GUIDE.md):

> The new popovers no longer include an arrow element. The s-popover--arrow css class has been removed,
> and any markup using it (e.g. \<div class="s-popover--arrow"\>\</div\>) should be deleted from the codebases
> as part of the migration.

This PR removes the arrow and centers the popover. This also changes how it looks on the legacy page, but since this is a low traffic page, it should be fine to change it in both. Additionally, it moves the  tooltip div outside of the table. Leaving it inside resulted in its corner being clipped by the next table column header.

Here is a screenshot of how it looks after the fix:

<img width="284" height="133" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5804e54c-fb2c-482c-a69e-d2092da4c445" />


## How to Test

Visit the "/admin/show-suspicious-votes" page. If doing this on local, most likely you won't have any suspicious votes. You can temporarily apply this diff to the `DeveloperController.Votes.cs` file to get a dev route that inserts suspicious votes on a random post and user.

```diff
