## Summary

This PR adds the ability for fragment proxies to forward `Set-Cookie` headers from upstream services to the client. This is controlled via a new configuration setting, `shouldForwardCookies`. 

By default, this setting is `false`, preserving existing behavior. It has been explicitly enabled for the `ai-assist` fragment to allow that service to manage state via cookies.

## How to Test
*I tried to get this deployed to main-test to test in a live environment, but the `deploy-to-google-cloud-ascn-dev` label does not seem to work.

To test locally:
- Update your local AskStack code to set a cookie.  
e.g.
```cs
app.Use(async (context, next) =>
{
    context.Response.Cookies.Append("MY-TEST", "DoesItWork");
    await next();
});
```
- Navigate to [https://meta.stackexchange.local/ai-assist](https://meta.stackexchange.local/ai-assist) and verify the cookie is forwarded through.

This PR is for [PRODPLAT-203](https://stackoverflow.atlassian.net/browse/PRODPLAT-203).

This PR adds a new `StatefulSet` to run the Outbox Monitor in the Stack Overflow deployment. This is so each pod gets a stable, predictable name with an index (e.g. `outbox-monitor-1`, `outbox-monitor-2`). This survives restarts and rescheduling.

The startup command for the pod grabs this index and sets it as a the `DistributedLock__ServiceInstanceIndex` environment variable. `DistributedLock__Strategy` is set to `Balanced`. 


[Here](https://github.com/StackEng/Octopus/pull/721) is the corresponding Octopus PR to set the variables for GCP. And [here](https://stackeng.octopus.app/app#/Spaces-1/projects/stackoverflow/deployments/releases/pr-25146/deployments/Deployments-328336) is a Octopus deploy to `ascn-dev` of this PR with the Octopus variables.

